---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import DuckDBQuery from '../components/DuckDBQuery.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Inline data queries"
  description="Query MIScope's published data bundles in your browser via DuckDB-WASM."
>
  <div class="post-header">
    <h1>Inline data queries</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Published findings carry their data. A <code>data-*</code> Release attaches the
      derived metrics behind a chart as Parquet; the box below runs SQL over that data
      <em>in your browser</em> — no install, no account. The query engine (DuckDB-WASM)
      loads on your first Run, and each query fetches only the bytes it touches.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Engine smoke (no remote data)</h2>
  <p>
    This box queries the engine itself — proof the in-browser SQL engine loads and runs.
    Edit the SQL and Run again.
  </p>

  <DuckDBQuery
    query={`SELECT i AS n, i * i AS square
FROM range(8) t(i)
ORDER BY n`}
    caption="A zero-data query against DuckDB-WASM. The engine is fetched from the CDN on the first Run, then reused."
  />

  <h2>Against a published bundle</h2>
  <p>
    Once a finding ships its <code>data-*</code> Release, an article points the same
    component at a Parquet asset URL and the reader queries it live. In MDX:
  </p>

  <pre class="usage"><code>{`import DuckDBQuery from '../../components/DuckDBQuery.astro';

<DuckDBQuery
  url="https://github.com/roaringsurfdev/MIScope/releases/download/data-ring-geometry-v1.0/shape_characterizations.parquet"
  table="shape_characterizations"
  query={\`SELECT variant_id, epoch, value AS circularity
FROM shape_characterizations
WHERE operation_type = 'circularity' AND epoch = 5000
ORDER BY circularity DESC\`}
  caption="Circularity ranked across variants at epoch 5000 — edit and re-run."
/>`}</code></pre>

  <p>
    A broken query is recoverable: the box stays editable and the error surfaces inline,
    so a reader can fix the SQL and Run again without leaving the page.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .usage {
    background: #f4f4f2;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
